    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-19T21:17:44+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-19T21:17:44+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-19T11:47:44Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-19T11:47:44Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred over NSW will extend a ridge westwards over SA during Saturday. A cold front will approach from the west late Saturday then move across SA on Sunday. Another high pressure system will move eastwards across waters to the south during Monday then over Victoria and the Tasman Sea on Tuesday. This high will extend a ridge westwards over SA ahead of a low pressure trough that is expected to move over the far west of SA during Wednesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-19T21:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-20T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-19T11:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-19T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Clear. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-20T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-21T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-19T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-20T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds northwest to northeasterly 30 to 45 km/h tending northwesterly in the middle of the day then tending northwest to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h in the late evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 12 and 18 with daytime temperatures reaching the mid to high 30s.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 8:50am to 3:20pm, UV Index predicted to reach 8 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-21T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-22T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-20T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-21T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Winds south to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h tending south to southeasterly 30 to 45 km/h during the morning then decreasing to 25 to 35 km/h in the middle of the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 10 and 18 with daytime temperatures reaching 21 to 35.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-22T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-23T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-21T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-22T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. The chance of morning frost south of Yunta. Winds southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 5 and 18 with daytime temperatures reaching 23 to 34.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-09-23T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-24T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-22T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-23T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny morning. The chance of a thunderstorm in the far northeast in the afternoon. Winds east to southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 6 and 18 with daytime temperatures reaching 27 to 35.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
